  "notes": [
    "Holds: a held_until timestamp on the seat (reads treat expired holds as free), or a key with a time-to-live in Redis. The expiry job keeps the data clean. The hold length is a product decision, often a few minutes.",
    "The price of a hold: while a seat is held nobody else can buy it. Too long a hold blocks seats for nothing; too short a hold and fans lose the seat while they type the card.",
    "The full video covers what happens when the payment arrives after the hold expired, and how to avoid charging twice."
  ],
